WEBVTT

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.280
Where would you recommend 
going for an end-of-the-year date?

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.410
That's obvious.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:20.830
The best choice is to go to the B-Project 
concert at the Japan Dome on December 31st.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.250
Ah! You're promoting your own event.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.190
No, I really do recommend it.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:28.200
You guys are putting a lot 
of energy into this one, right?

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:32.060
It's a summary of our progress 
up until this point.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.260
Come see this concert,

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.390
and I think you'll get a sense of the 
direction we're heading in the future.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.720
I look forward to that.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.850
Too bad, though.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:45.940
Haven't tickets for the concert already sold out?

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.980
That's right. Thanks, everyone.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.700
Whoops! We're almost out of time.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.890
Finally, Kitakado-kun, do you have 
a message for the B-Project fans

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:56.950
who will be attending?

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:01.340
Come catch us at the Japan Dome.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:32.930
Here you go.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.880
One extra large katsudon.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.710
That looks delicious.

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:38.630
Thanks for the food.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:42.750
It's so good.

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:47.220
I knew that would happen.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.730
It's so good.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:53.760
Huh? Ken-Ken, you're not eating?

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:58.490
Yeah. It's easy to consume 
excess calories around New Year's.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.740
It's better to restrict 
yourself as much as you can.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.240
You might be right.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:05.380
I love omu-rice.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.520
Yuta, are you even listening?

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:13.260
Well, if it isn't B-Pro.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.950
Ninomiya-san. It's been a while.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.660
Thank you for working with us 
on the curry commercial.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.720
Please, please. Stay seated.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:26.490
Anyway, B-Pro has become really popular.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:29.680
It hasn't been that long 
since we filmed the commercial.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:33.160
I can't believe you're performing 
at the Japan Dome already.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.300
Thank you. We have you to thank for that.

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.610
I didn't do anything.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.950
I hope it'll be an amazing concert.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:43.840
I'll send you an invitation.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:44.570
No need.

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:47.780
I already bought tickets for myself.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.200
That's the first time 
I've seen tickets to our show.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.620
B-Pro's getting a lot of 
international attention, too.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:55.750
Make sure the concert is a success.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.880
We will. Thank you.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.420
I'm looking forward to it.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:03.610
By the way, Tsubasa...

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.600
Have you met with Yashamaru-san since then?

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:14.490
But he's reading his "Join" messages, right?

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:15.390
Yes.

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:19.550
The president isn't having trouble 
getting in touch with him.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:23.150
Maybe you just have bad timing, Sumisora?

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:26.160
That's probably it.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:27.280
Here you go.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.000
Hey, that's...

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.490
The super huge baumkuchen you requested.

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:36.670
Normally, we don't accept personal requests...

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:41.510
but Yashamaru-san begged us to make it.

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:44.910
What? Yashamaru-san comes here?

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:46.640
Yeah, all the time.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:50.680
But he always gulps down 
his donburi and leaves right away.

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:52.930
He must be busy.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:56.210
Looks like we're just missing him.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:59.520
Well, Yashamaru-san is always busy.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:05.530
But if he ordered a baumkuchen for us, 
then he must be thinking of us.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.950
But it's just for Ryu-chan.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:10.690
Ma'am, I'd like a rainbow pudding.

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:14.600
You should ask Yashamaru-san 
for that, not me.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.040
No way!

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:20.950
We'd better work as hard as Yashamaru-san.

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:23.620
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:27.430
In any case, we should put everything 
we have towards the Japan Dome concert.

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:31.510
Yeah. We should think about 
B-Pro's future after that, too.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.180
After the concert, huh?

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:40.420
Maybe Yashamaru-san's busy because 
he's planning B-Pro's next big project.

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:41.860
Our next big project?

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:42.320
Yeah.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:47.070
Are we going to do a 
collaboration with Mamirin?

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.130
Probably not.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:51.280
Why not? You can't be sure.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:52.740
Maybe we'll perform overseas.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.950
What? I'd better study some English then.

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:57.710
Even though you still need 
to work on your Japanese?

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:01.690
Maybe we'll be recording an album.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:03.630
An album, huh? That would be nice.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:05.590
Huh?

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:07.470
What?

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.990
Unfortunately, I haven't heard 
anything about making an album.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:13.220
What?

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:18.480
B-But the song we'll be debuting 
at the Dome is coming along nicely.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.140
Yeah, you're right.

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:22.340
Our new song is awesome.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:24.150
It's the centerpiece of the concert.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.350
I'm hyped to do the recording.

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:27.240
Yeah.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:33.700
<i>Run & Gun Shoot now along the light</i>

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:39.120
<i>Make the shot and head towards 
the future that lies beyond</i>

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:45.130
<i>Time will tell, face forward and 
start running. Don't look back!</i>

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:56.340
<i>I'll burn the first incredible 
sight I see into my eyes</i>

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:57.140
There. That settles that.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:02.050
Hey, Tsubasa-chan. Could we the discuss 
the harmonizing melody of that section?

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.750
What? Oh, um...

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:08.190
I'm sorry. Could you play it again?

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:11.960
Oh, sorry. Why don't we take a break then?

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:13.820
S-Sorry.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:14.660
Kaneshiro-kun,

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:16.800
<i>we're taking a short break.</i>

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:17.910
Okay.

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:21.800
Don't let this get you down.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:26.150
Compared to Yashamaru-san, 
I'm barely even trying.

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:26.910
What?

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:29.020
Isn't that what you're thinking?

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:30.750
Ryuji-kun.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.140
Let me see your hands.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:32.710
My hands?

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:34.140
Just do it.

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:38.130
I'm making an exception for you.

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:40.590
You look like you need 
something sweet right now.

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:42.770
Th-Thank you.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:45.500
Sumisora, don't you think 
you're pushing yourself too hard?

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.270
No, I'm totally fine.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:50.530
I understand why you're 
working so hard, though.

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:53.850
After all, you've got excellent 
composers working on the song.

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:56.450
I'm impressed you were able to hire them.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.000
Yashamaru-san arranged it for us.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.940
I'm not surprised.

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:03.800
He has all kinds of connections.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:08.320
Once this song is released, B-Project 
will achieve even more success.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:09.800
Right, Tsubasa-chan?

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:10.800
Yes.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.930
Sumisora, how did it go?

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:16.060
Your singing is always 
fantastic, Kaneshiro-san.

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:18.650
That's not what I meant.

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:21.380
I'm asking about the arrangement 
I asked you to make.

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:25.270
Oh, I just sent an e-mail about that.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:30.840
Hey, this hasn't been sent yet.

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:31.690
What?

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:33.210
There was a transmission error.

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:36.590
Huh? Maybe I got the address wrong.

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:38.110
You...

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:39.410
Sorry.

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:41.540
You must be tired.

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:44.080
Sweets are great for when you're tired.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:48.020
You just need to finish the 
arrangement by next week, right?

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:49.800
You should take a break.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:54.180
I can't. Tomorrow, we have an all-day 
shoot related to the Dome concert.

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:58.470
I'll do whatever I can in the meantime.

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:03.310
Good morning.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:04.830
Good morning.

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:06.190
Sumisora-san.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:08.560
Do you have a minute?

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:12.080
The makeup artist isn't here?

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:14.820
No. When were they supposed to arrive?

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:18.910
I told them to be here 
thirty minutes before we started.

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:20.950
That's odd.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.320
Let me check in with them.

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:27.420
This is Sumisora of Gandara.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:28.960
I'm calling about today's makeup.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:31.650
What? A different location?

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:32.960
What does that...

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:34.740
They hung up.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:35.910
What did they say?

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:38.790
They said they can't help 
with B-Pro's makeup anymore.

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:41.720
Don't they work with you exclusively?

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:47.200
Yes, but apparently, our contract expired.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:51.210
That's a problem. 
We can't push the shoot back.

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:53.730
I'll try asking some other makeup artists.

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:56.740
Could you help us right away?

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.740
Yes, of course.

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:02.740
I'm sorry. Excuse me.

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:08.570
It's no use. It's impossible 
to get someone on such short notice.

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:09.310
Good work.

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:11.460
Thank you.

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:17.300
I've been looking forward to today's shoot.

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:20.300
After this video, our new song...

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:25.810
Hikarun, I have no idea 
what you're trying to say.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:29.780
You're trying to say this video is important 
for promoting our new song, right?

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:33.830
Sumisora, how's the arrangement coming along?

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:35.840
I sent the e-mail again.

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:38.700
I should be getting a response soon.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:39.700
<b>The E-mail Could Not Be Delivered</b>

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:39.700
Huh?

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:41.920
What did they say?

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:45.890
Hey, Sumisora.

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:48.100
Something's wrong.

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:48.960
What?

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:55.710
I think the shoot went pretty well.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.840
I'm excited to see the finished product.

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:00.000
Look, Tsubasa-chan.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.550
Don't I look awesome from this angle?

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:05.740
Hey, Tsubasa-chan.

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:07.320
Tsubasa-chan!

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:10.560
Oh, y-yeah, you do.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:18.020
I'm sure the fans will love—

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:20.690
She froze.

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:22.700
Does she need to be restarted?

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:24.890
Is this...

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:25.830
What's wrong?

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:27.740
I'm sorry. I'm opening a window.

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:34.640
<i>Run & Gun Shoot now along the light</i>

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:39.990
<i>Make the shot and head towards 
the future that lies beyond</i>

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:36.040
This is...

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:38.090
Our new song.

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:40.470
But we haven't announced it yet.

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:46.170
<i>Time will tell, face forward and 
start running. Don't look back!</i>

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:42.260
Why?

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:51.310
What's going on?

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:53.900
I don't know, either.

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:56.270
Where is Yashamaru-san?

00:11:56.660 --> 00:11:59.700
He's been e-mailing
me instructions for work...

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:02.780
but he won't answer my calls or messages.

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:06.910
Why don't we check with 
Uta Hime Lunch's agency?

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:08.480
I called several times,

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:11.320
but they can't talk to us since the 
employee responsible for them isn't there.

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:14.110
It was supposed to be our
concert's centerpiece.

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:17.420
We'll have to give up on debuting a new song.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:21.460
But won't that change 
the concert program quite a bit?

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:23.680
We'll have to switch around the blocks.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.600
And our choreography, too.

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:28.090
What? Even after we learned it?

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:31.930
I'm not sure there's time to come up 
with a performance to take its place.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:34.220
Whining about it won't get us anywhere.

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:35.560
We have to think.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:36.480
Please wait a moment.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:37.190
What?

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:39.570
Let's make a new song.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:40.920
What?

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:44.040
Sumisora, what are you talking about?

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:46.070
There are only two weeks until the show.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:49.580
I'm not sure it's possible 
to make one in time.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.660
We can't know that unless we try.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:52.580
Tsubasa.

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:57.700
It would be easy to pretend nothing 
happened and put on a concert.

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:01.330
Maybe I'm being impertinent.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:08.590
But I want to show everything B-Pro 
has done, and will do, at the concert.

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:14.020
So we need a new song
to perform at the concert.

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:19.710
As the individual who's been B-Project's 
A&R until this point, that's how I feel.

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:22.100
What do the rest of you think?

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:25.670
Tsubasa's right.

00:13:26.230 --> 00:13:27.360
Kitakado-san.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:31.620
The Japan Dome is our second start.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:38.880
Yeah. We can't compromise, give up, 
or stand onstage while feeling stalled.

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:42.370
I'm sure our fans want the same thing.

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:46.470
We'll have to write a super cool song.

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:49.260
Hikaru, you're not writing anything.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:54.530
I know it's crazy, but I feel 
like we can do it. It's strange.

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:57.020
Maybe this is one of your powers, Tsubasa.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:57.890
What?

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:01.860
Oh, well. The lack of sleep 
is going to be terrible for my skin.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:03.170
But we have to do it.

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:05.860
Ken-Ken, you're feeling motivated.

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:06.820
Good for you.

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:08.900
Are you making fun of me?

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:10.450
This is no joke.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:11.740
Gochin?

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:14.540
We can't let it end like this.

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:17.370
Let's make a new song.

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:18.750
Yeah.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:20.510
Guys.

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:21.980
Please believe in us.

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:25.030
I promise, promise, promise 
we'll make it in time.

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:25.510
Yeah.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.760
It won't be easy.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:32.710
I guess we have to accept it.

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:36.770
Yeah. We'll find the right 
musical staff to back you up.

00:14:37.090 --> 00:14:39.270
All right. Give it everything 
you've got, boys.

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:41.270
Yeah!

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:46.960
I know this is sudden, but could 
you write us a song by next week?

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:48.780
No, we can't use something 
you've already written.

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:51.030
We need a new one.

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:55.010
I need an arrangement.

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:58.040
Something fast and upbeat.

00:14:58.340 --> 00:14:59.790
In three days.

00:15:16.610 --> 00:15:17.850
Guys.

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:25.110
Well?

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:27.850
Don't you think it's better than before?

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:29.890
It's way better.

00:15:29.890 --> 00:15:31.820
I'm super excited.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:34.740
It's incredible. I can't believe we've 
made this much progress so quickly.

00:15:35.010 --> 00:15:38.050
The last remaining problem is the lyrics.

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:39.580
Lyrics for this song...

00:15:39.930 --> 00:15:43.580
<i>Who can write lyrics to express 
what we're feeling now?</i>

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:45.510
Let's write the lyrics together.

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:47.940
This song is our song.

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:50.840
What it needs is our words.

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:53.720
I think we should write them, too.

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:56.180
You're right. I want
to try writing some lyrics.

00:15:56.590 --> 00:15:57.970
No, I want to.

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:00.100
Looks like we actually agree sometimes.

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:02.850
What do you think, Tsubasa?

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:06.230
What does our A&R think?

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:09.990
Write us something great, please.

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:13.740
First, we need to decide on a concept.

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:16.320
What impression did you guys 
have about the song?

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:18.470
I thought it was incredible.

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:20.510
You sound like a child.

00:16:20.510 --> 00:16:22.330
But that's what I thought.

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:24.620
I felt like I could see the future.

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:28.090
It was like new possibilities 
were spreading before us.

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:30.420
It's more perfect than 
anything we've done so far.

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:34.370
Yeah. With this song, no one can beat us.

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:36.680
No one can beat us, huh?

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.680
Yeah. It makes me feel invincible.

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:41.680
What?

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:44.260
Huh? Did I say something wrong?

00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:45.980
Osari, what did you just say?

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:47.940
Was I wrong?

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:49.080
Before that.

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:51.360
That it makes me feel invincible.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.440
That's it!

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:53.320
What?

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:54.990
Nice, Hikaru.

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:56.410
Huh? What?

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:57.370
Invincible!

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:01.120
All right! The song's concept 
will be "invincible!"

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:06.790
Invincible, huh? What's invincible?

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:07.750
Sweet things!

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.120
I knew you'd say that.

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:11.150
Ryu-chan, what's invincible to you?

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:13.510
Maybe human connections.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:16.150
No fair. Only your idea is cool.

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:17.510
It's not unfair at all.

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:21.510
You could say episode 32 
of <i>Witch Girl Mamirin</i>,

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:25.620
"Vice Principal: Friend or Foe," is invincible.

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:27.050
Right, Momotasu?

00:17:27.050 --> 00:17:29.800
You've shown me this episode ten times.

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:32.340
Why are you even watching this here?

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:34.030
To learn about invincibility.

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:36.440
Watch it in your own rooms.

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:40.010
Actually, our leader's eyes 
have been so cold lately.

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:44.000
I see. So Kazuna's eyes are 
the most invincible of all.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:48.750
<b>Ganjara Ramen</b>

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:47.410
This shop's ramen is the 
most invincible of all.

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:48.750
Definitely.

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:51.090
Can't you guys take this seriously?

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:52.420
We are.

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:55.390
How? And today, we're splitting the bill.

00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:56.950
What? No way.

00:17:56.950 --> 00:17:58.010
Isn't that normal?

00:17:58.960 --> 00:17:59.760
What?

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:04.140
Maybe these times we spend 
goofing around are the most invincible.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.010
What?

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:08.870
Tatsu, that was great.

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:12.440
Friends. Friendship.

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:14.650
Family. Life.

00:18:15.050 --> 00:18:16.650
They're all invincible.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.660
And miracles.

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:20.160
Miracles?

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:22.740
The ten of us came together miraculously,

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:25.540
and we have the greatest A&R.

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:30.350
Yeah. We are invincible.

00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:34.410
I finished making arrangements 
for their outfits.

00:18:34.410 --> 00:18:36.020
That's everything I can do today.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:38.880
I should give this to them.

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:43.890
Sorry for stopping by so late.

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:45.620
What are you doing here?

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:48.020
I received the documentation 
for tomorrow's location.

00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:50.230
Thanks.

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:52.870
Where's Hikaru-kun?

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:55.250
He's taking a shower.

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:03.040
How did the lyrics go?

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:06.520
Kaneshiro's putting something 
together based on our thoughts.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:09.000
They might even be done by tomorrow.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:10.920
Really? That's amazing.

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:14.420
Speaking of tomorrow, it's Christmas Eve.

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:16.340
What? Oh, right.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:17.750
You didn't notice?

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:18.800
No.

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:21.050
Well, you have been busy.

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:25.770
I hope the lyrics to our new song 
can be our Christmas present to you.

00:19:25.770 --> 00:19:30.390
What? I've never received 
such a wonderful present.

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:34.460
Naturally, Momotasu will deliver them 
to you in a Santa Claus costume.

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:35.400
I'm not doing that.

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:38.900
I really am excited to see them, though.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:40.750
Sumisora-san, do you want some coffee?

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:42.590
Oh, I'll make it.

00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:46.620
That's all right. 
Our exhausted A&R should rest.

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:55.460
Nothing beats a cola after a bath.

00:19:56.180 --> 00:19:56.920
Hikaru, wait.

00:19:57.210 --> 00:19:58.670
Sumisora-san's in there.

00:19:58.890 --> 00:20:00.670
Huh? Tsubasa-chan.

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.930
What are you doing here so late at night?

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:04.810
H-Hikaru-kun!

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:07.030
Um... The documents...

00:20:07.030 --> 00:20:07.930
Oh, right.

00:20:08.300 --> 00:20:10.300
I can't believe you're working this late.

00:20:14.490 --> 00:20:16.150
No!

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:16.150
No!

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:18.500
Th-That was rather unfortunate.

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:19.650
I'm sorry.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:23.270
I'm always telling you 
not to walk around naked.

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:29.470
Merry Christmas.

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:32.660
Nobody wants a present like that.

00:20:44.550 --> 00:20:46.430
Tsubasa, what do you think?

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:50.430
Huh? Was it not good?

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:53.560
It's incredible.

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:55.560
All right!

00:20:57.570 --> 00:21:03.110
I can't say it that loudly, but I think 
this is even better than the other song.

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:04.330
Isn't it?

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:07.640
All right! Now we have nothing to fear!

00:21:07.640 --> 00:21:10.410
The Dome concert is sure to be a success.

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:13.370
Yes. Just leave the rest to me.

00:21:14.030 --> 00:21:16.120
I promise it'll be a success.

00:21:16.610 --> 00:21:20.800
I can't believe Tsubasa 
can speak so confidently now.

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:22.380
I never thought it would happen.

00:21:32.230 --> 00:21:33.810
It's all thanks to you.

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:37.690
<b>Yashamaru Sakutaro</b>

00:21:38.410 --> 00:21:39.950
It's from Yashamaru-san.

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:42.400
So Yashamaru-san's alive.

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:45.060
Aren't you glad he contacted
you, Tsubasa-chan?

00:21:45.060 --> 00:21:45.790
Yes.

00:21:45.790 --> 00:21:48.230
We'd better tell him about the song.

00:21:48.230 --> 00:21:49.950
What did Yashamaru-san say?

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:51.200
<b>Turn on the TV.</b>

00:21:53.490 --> 00:21:55.200
<b>Suddenly Transferred to
Highedge Records</b>

00:21:57.350 --> 00:21:58.830
What is this?

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:01.590
<b>Suddenly Transferred to
Highedge Records</b>

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:02.460
<b>What?!

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:11.720
<b>Suddenly Transferred to
Highedge Records</b>

00:22:07.610 --> 00:22:08.510
What does this mean?

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:10.360
No one told us anything about this.

00:22:10.360 --> 00:22:12.280
Sumisora, call Yashamaru-san.

00:22:12.910 --> 00:22:13.700
Got it.

00:22:15.790 --> 00:22:20.050
<i>The number you called 
is not currently in use.</i>

00:22:20.050 --> 00:22:20.730
What?

00:23:55.850 --> 00:23:56.880
Sweet dreams.

00:23:56.880 --> 00:23:57.840
Hope you have them.

00:23:57.840 --> 00:23:58.780
Good night.
